{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1793400055,"nonce":"2TJSVTWdgCjv0OdcwiuiGyAgewY=","message":"Root cause found and fixed. It was not the ashui pin and not the session or the rayzor binary. The rebuilt bundle shipped stale window libraries: ashui/tests/bin/web/hlwindow-web (xwindow.mjs and xwindow.wasm) was last built against xwindow 53d8f63 (Oct 22), before xwindow f42bd37 'Wake browser work without redrawing' and 1240e4c 'Consume browser defaults for application shortcuts' (Oct 25), which hlwindow already pins. Without the wake support (RUNTIME_WAKE and APPLICATION_WAKE in xwindow.mjs and the matching wasm side) work finished on background threads does not wake the page loop, so session replies, extension host calls and file reads wait for an unrelated wake: the rayzor extension never reached registerServer, the host was killed and respawned at about 60 s, the Build page sat on Loading build.hxml, and the Markdown extension and previews did not load. The committed bundle had the right files because they were built after Oct 25; scripts/build-web.sh copied whatever was in the cache and never refreshed it, so my rebuild overwrote them. Fix: rebuilt hlwindow-web and hlwgpu-web with ashui's own helper (web_libraries; stamp now xwindow 1240e4c), rebuilt the site bundle (the new xwindow.mjs is byte-identical to the committed one), and made build-web.sh run the same stamp check first (a no-op in about a quarter of a second when current). Verified headless against the live 8731 session: the page answers rayde.settings.get in about 10 ms, registerServer at 2.12 s, rayzor lsp spawned at 2.16 s (was never); tests/web/builtins.mjs passes with rayzor, diagnostics, git and markdown all true; tests/web/public-demo.mjs passes. Not directly tested: the Build settings page itself, which loads build.hxml through a background worker and the same completion path. Commits 3fcfc15 and 210350b. The earlier hypothesis about the ashui pin and 19 commits was wrong; the pin stays.","files":null}]}